00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.800
Because, as it turns out, in Japan, that&nbsp;
has famously been isolated for large parts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:39.680
of its history, kissing has not really been a&nbsp;
THING, until quite recently. If you know a bit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:45.520
of Japanese or have watched enough anime, you’ll&nbsp;
probably know that the Japanese word for ‘Kiss’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:52.160
is actually JUST the katakana word Kizu,&nbsp;
so simply copied over from English.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:57.840
Now in fact there is a Japanase word for the&nbsp;
act itself dating back to the Edo-period,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:09.840
that looks like this and literally&nbsp;
