00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:16.240
Actually maybe not so ew after all. The catch&nbsp;
here however, is that this was simply considered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:23.840
to be part of *** and not a separate concept&nbsp;
in itself. And so it took some more time until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:31.760
kissing finally got its own specific word. And&nbsp;
by some more time, I mean the early 20th century.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:37.520
The crux of all this is that kissing in&nbsp;
the classically romantic sense of the west&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:44.240
has only reached Japan very very recently.&nbsp;
And, as my Japanese friends confirmed when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:49.360
I asked them about it, even though kissing&nbsp;
has been widely normalized today, it still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:54.640
carries a bit of this sexual connotation, and&nbsp;
is considered to be a very intimate thing to do.

00:05:54.640 --> 00:06:00.320
There actually is a related concept in Japan,&nbsp;
that I think explains pretty well how this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:06.480
history influences the use of kissing in Anime.&nbsp;
PDA. Now you might or might not have heard this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:12.080
term before. If you have. Congratulations, you&nbsp;
can put a cookie emote in the comments. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:17.920
if you’re like me when I first moved to Japan&nbsp;
3 years ago and have absolutely no idea was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:26.960
this means PDA stands for public display of&nbsp;
affection, and is not limited to just Japan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:32.240
With this phrase many East Asian countries&nbsp;
describe any sort of public physical contact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:37.280
between two people who are attracted to&nbsp;
each other. This of course includes kissing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:43.440
but also supposedly ‘harmless’ things like hugging&nbsp;
or holding hands. While for westerners it’s pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:49.520
normal, if admittedly at times a bit annoying to&nbsp;
see a couple go at it in public or simply cuddle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:55.440
together, Japanese people tend to feel quite&nbsp;
uncomfortable about this stuff. It’s something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.440 --> 00:07:02.960
meant to be done in private. And this ALSO goes&nbsp;
for PDA on TV. And Anime is no exception here.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:09.200
How then am I supposed to get any real romance&nbsp;
in these stories, you may rightfully ask.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:15.600
The answer is, it’s already there. The&nbsp;
real secret to understanding romance and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:20.880
relationships in Anime is to understand&nbsp;
how relationships tend to work in Japan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:25.040
In most western countries a&nbsp;
relationship often starts with a kiss,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:30.160
which is why we love to see it so much in film.&nbsp;
Then the couple has time to get to know each other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:35.440
better and form an emotional relationship&nbsp;
as well. The BIG cultural difference here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:41.280
is that Japanese relationships tend to work the&nbsp;
other way around. Two people start, you spend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:46.960
a lot of time building a strong emotional bond&nbsp;
and learning what the other person is all about.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:52.960
This emotional tension keeps building&nbsp;
until one formally confesses their feelings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:58.640
and hopes for the best that the other person&nbsp;
return them. Once you have reached KISSING level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:05.280
the relationship usually has already reached&nbsp;
a pretty serious and intimate stage. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:09.840
of course there are western couples who&nbsp;
date for a long time before ever kissing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:14.800
and Japanese people who just like to&nbsp;
make out at a bar. But in general,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:20.160
it’s undeniable that there is a fundamental&nbsp;
difference in the meaning of a kiss.

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:25.680
In other words, the reason that there seems&nbsp;
to be no kissing in anime is not because it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:32.080
meant for kids or anything, but because kissing&nbsp;
plays a very different role in Japanese romance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:36.800
than it does in the west. Now, thanks to&nbsp;
the internet and globalization in general,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.760
this will surely change in the future - probably.

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:44.880
But for now, if you want to pick up on the&nbsp;
actually surprisingly intense romance in Anime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:50.320
no matter the genre, make sure to look for&nbsp;
these smaller gestures that mean so much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:55.200
more to Japanese people. A flirty conversation,&nbsp;
a bump of the hand or watching a sunset together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.840 --> 00:09:01.600
actually mean way more to these characters&nbsp;
and a Japanese audience than you might expect.

